{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ConjLeptonTowerHNPlus1Branching","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ConjLeptonTowerHNPlus1Branching","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.lepton_xi_electron_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.lepton_xi_electron_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L210-L212","doc":"**THEOREM (electron ξ_1 calibration convention).** `ξ_1 = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.lepton_xi_tau_eq_reduced_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.lepton_xi_tau_eq_reduced_form","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L191-L208","doc":"**THEOREM (tau ξ_3 closed-form reduction).**\n`ξ_3 = [5]_q · [3]_q / [6]_q = [5]_q / ([2]_q · (1+h²))`.\n\n**Non-vanishing hypotheses:** `[6]_q ≠ 0` (LHS denominator) plus\n`[2]_q ≠ 0` and `1 + h² ≠ 0` (RHS denominator factors). All hold\nat the substrate `q_0 ≈ 1.110` and over any field of characteristic\nzero where `q` is not a primitive 12th root of unity.\nPer gemini-code-assist PR #1254 review. The underlying identity\n`tau_xi_cross_mul` needs none of them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.lepton_xi_muon_eq_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.lepton_xi_muon_eq_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L173-L189","doc":"**THEOREM (muon ξ_2 closed-form algebraic identity).**\n`ξ_2 = [3]_q · [2]_q / [4]_q = (3+h²)/(2+h²)`.\n\n**Non-vanishing hypotheses:** `[4]_q ≠ 0` (LHS denominator) and\n`2 + h² ≠ 0` (RHS denominator) ensure the equality is non-vacuous.\nBoth hold at the substrate `q_0 ≈ 1.110` and over any field of\ncharacteristic zero where `q` is not a primitive 8th root of unity.\nPer gemini-code-assist PR #1254 review. The underlying identity\n`muon_xi_cross_mul` needs neither hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.lepton_xi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.lepton_xi","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L156-L171","doc":"Lepton-tower ξ_m structural factor (without the 1/ℏ_q² substrate\nscalar; the full closure is `lepton_xi · (1/ℏ_q²)`).\n\nThe unifying formula is ξ_m = [2m-1]_q · [m]_q / [2m]_q:\n- electron: degenerate calibration unit (ξ_1 = 1 by convention)\n- muon: ξ_2 = [3]_q · [2]_q / [4]_q\n- tau:  ξ_3 = [5]_q · [3]_q / [6]_q\n\nAlgebraic identity (closed h-form):\n- muon: ξ_2 = (3+h²) / (2+h²)  — proved via lepton_xi_muon_eq_closed_form\n- tau:  ξ_3 = [5]_q / ([2]_q · (1+h²))  — proved via lepton_xi_tau_eq_reduced_form\n","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching","label":"conj:lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.tau_xi_cross_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.tau_xi_cross_mul","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L130-L144","doc":"**THEOREM (tau ξ₃ structural identity, division-free).**\nThe cross-multiplied content of `ξ_3 = [5]_q · [3]_q / [6]_q\n= [5]_q / ([2]_q · (1 + h²))`:\n\n  [5]_q · [3]_q · ([2]_q · (1 + h²)) = [5]_q · [6]_q.\n\nHolds over any commutative ring, with no non-vanishing hypotheses.\n\nThe categorical derivation (why the symmetric q-bracket form\nappears, and how 10_43's amphichirality + hook-length pattern\nselects it) is open work for Option E (Kashiwara crystal, PR #1252). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.br6_eq_br2_br3_times_one_plus_h_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.br6_eq_br2_br3_times_one_plus_h_sq","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L117-L128","doc":"**THEOREM (tau structural reduction).** `[6]_q = [2]_q · [3]_q · (1 + h²)`.\nMirrors `bracket6_eq_bracket2_bracket3_times_one_plus_h_sq` from\n`three-halves-structural-factor.lean`. The fundamental identity\nbehind the tau amphichiral closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.muon_xi_cross_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.muon_xi_cross_mul","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L100-L115","doc":"**THEOREM (muon ξ₂ structural identity, division-free).**\nThe cross-multiplied content of `ξ_2 = [3]_q · [2]_q / [4]_q\n= (3 + h²)/(2 + h²)`:\n\n  [3]_q · [2]_q · (2 + h²) = (3 + h²) · [4]_q.\n\nHolds over any commutative ring, with no non-vanishing hypotheses.\n\nThe categorical derivation (why this form arises from the per-braid\nmass tower at the H_3 substrate via the conj's \"(m+1, 1) std irrep\nin S_{m+2}\" identification) remains open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.two_plus_h_sq_mul_br2_eq_br4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.two_plus_h_sq_mul_br2_eq_br4","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L93-L98","doc":"`(2 + h²) · [2]_q = [4]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.br3_eq_three_plus_h_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.br3_eq_three_plus_h_sq","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L86-L91","doc":"`[3]_q = 3 + h²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.br6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.br6","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L79-L82","doc":"q-bracket [6]_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.br5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.br5","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L75-L77","doc":"q-bracket [5]_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.br4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.br4","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L71-L73","doc":"q-bracket [4]_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.br3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.br3","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L68-L69","doc":"q-bracket [3]_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.br2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.br2","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L65-L66","doc":"q-bracket [2]_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.heckeH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.heckeH","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L61-L63","doc":"Hecke amplitude h = q - q⁻¹ (mirrors definition in\n`three-halves-structural-factor.lean`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.instDecidableEqLeptonIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.instDecidableEqLeptonIndex","kind":"instance","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.LeptonIndex.tau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.LeptonIndex.tau","kind":"ctor","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.LeptonIndex.muon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.LeptonIndex.muon","kind":"ctor","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.LeptonIndex.electron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.LeptonIndex.electron","kind":"ctor","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.LeptonIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonTowerHnPlus1.LeptonIndex","kind":"inductive","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-lepton-tower-h-n-plus-1-branching.lean#L52-L57","doc":"Lepton tower index. ","signatureChunk":0}]}